<title>CANADA: StatsCan survey sees March unemployment at 9.7 pct.</title>
<headline>StatsCan survey sees March unemployment at 9.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Statistics Canada survey of analysts forecast Canadian unemployment to remain flat at 9.7 percent in March from February.</p>
<p>The survey also forecast that consumer prices would rise in March by 2.1 pct from a year earlier.</p>
<p>The survey forecast gross domestic product to rise 0.2 percent in February from January.</p>
<p>The economists also forecast merchandise exports for February at C$23.3 billion, and imports of C$21.4 billion.</p>
<p>The agency on average surveys 17 economists each month.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
<p>	     -</p>
